      "widgets_values": [
        "subject_definitions:\n<Picture 1> is a character turnaround of a young East Asian woman: shoulder-length wavy brown hair, a small sparkling bow hair clip on her left side, a cropped cream tweed jacket with gold buttons and a pearl-and-gold bow brooch, a matching cream rib-knit top, a long pleated light-peach midi skirt, and cream pointed-toe block-heel pumps. Use the close-up portrait panel for face identity. Ignore any red occlusion mark on the front full-body panel. Do not copy the studio gray background.\n<Video 1> is the source video for this recast: a ~5–6s portrait 9:16 studio clip. The original performer is a young Asian woman with long dark wavy hair and bangs, gold hoop earrings, a gold pendant, and a short emerald-green spaghetti-strap slip dress. She is the person to REPLACE.\n\nsummary:\n[video editing + character replacement] Recast <Video 1>. Keep the white seamless studio, high-angle medium-close camera, timing, hair-whip / sway motion, and the upbeat electronic dance track. Replace ONLY the performer with the woman from <Picture 1> in the cream tweed outfit. Do not keep the green dress, gold hoops, gold pendant, long bangs, or the original face.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Picture 1>: fully_preserved — face, hairstyle (shoulder-length wavy brown hair + bow clip), body proportions, and the cream tweed outfit. Not the gray studio backdrop. Ignore the red mark.\n<Video 1>: fully_preserved — white seamless background, high-angle medium-close framing, subtle camera track, motion beats, and lighting. Do NOT keep the original performer's identity or clothes.\n<Video 1> soundtrack: partially_copy — reuse the fast electronic dance music; no new dialogue.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video is a portrait 9:16 recast of <Video 1> on a plain white seamless studio backdrop, high-angle medium-close, camera gently tracking.\n[Shot 1] 0.0s: the woman from <Picture 1> leans slightly forward, looking up into the lens, same pose as <Video 1>.\n0.0–1.0s: she swiftly turns her head to her left (screen right), whipping her brown hair, matching <Video 1>'s timing.\n~2.0s: she snaps her head back to face the camera, playful smile, hair settling.\n~3.0s: she looks down and aside while swaying her torso, still wearing the cream tweed jacket and pleated midi skirt from <Picture 1>.\n4.0–6.0s: she glances up to her right (screen left), then returns her gaze to camera with a gentle rhythmic bounce, holding that state to the end.\nThroughout, her face and outfit stay locked to <Picture 1>; blocking, camera, and white studio stay locked to <Video 1>.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nContinuous upbeat electronic dance music copied from <Video 1>. No dialogue. No extra SFX.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nKeep <Video 1>'s EDM track; do not replace it.\n"
      ],
